From 466259968216f01527e888d7e9c23e5960548937 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ilya84 <kacnep.0000@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:32:33 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] los-tv: auto-install, TV settings focus, configurable check
 schedule

Add an opt-in auto-install mode to the existing Updater settings: the
periodic check worker downloads/streams the newest build, the service
promotes itself to foreground for background installs, and
UPDATED_NEED_REBOOT either posts the usual notification or reboots when
auto-reboot is enabled. Both settings default to off.

Fix the Updater settings screen on TV: use SettingsScaffold with the same
fillMaxSize + padding + verticalScroll layout as the main Updates screen,
and move initial focus from the top-left back button to the first
preference. Without this no preference had focus and OK/Enter activated
Back instead of the selected setting.

Replace the periodic "every N days" check with a configurable schedule:
daily, weekly (weekday) or monthly (day of month) at HH:MM, with minutes
in 5-minute steps, a next-run summary and a catch-up note. WorkManager
one-time work is scheduled at the next run with unique generation names;
a missed or failed check is retried about 12 minutes after boot/failure
(up to 3 attempts), and pending catch-up state survives reboot. Remove
the old CheckInterval model, migrating the legacy check_interval key.

Improve update notifications: a successful install always posts
"update installed, reboot required"; tapping the notification opens a
RebootActivity confirmation dialog instead of just the Updater screen.
Failure notifications (download error, verification failed, install
failed, post-reboot install failure) are posted only when auto-install
is enabled; with auto-install off the error stays in the Updater UI and
tapping the notification (when present) opens Updater.

Change-Id: Ia4b15cfc610cb42e4a63a790531f2e196d96d4f1
